# Generic Code Agent

Language-agnostic codefly agent providing baseline filesystem, git, and search operations for any repository.

## Capabilities

- **File operations**: ReadFile, WriteFile, CreateFile, DeleteFile, MoveFile, ListFiles
- **Search**: Full-text search (ripgrep or in-memory regex)
- **Git**: GitLog, GitDiff, GitShow, GitBlame
- **Edit**: ApplyEdit (smart find/replace)
- **Project info**: File hashes, directory structure

## What it does NOT provide

- No LSP (language server protocol)
- No AST analysis
- No call graph
- No symbol extraction
- No language-specific build/test/lint

This agent is the **fallback** when no language-specific agent (Go, Python, etc.) is available.
Every language-specific agent inherits all of these operations automatically.

## Container images and SBOM evidence

This agent produces **no runtime image**. It is a passive toolbox: it registers
no Builder and advertises no BUILDER capability, so it emits no runtime, init,
migration, or sidecar image for a scanner to inventory.

Under the shared Codefly SBOM contract that status is `NO_IMAGE` — a service
that legitimately ships nothing to scan — and it is deliberately distinct from
an agent whose image SBOM support is simply unimplemented. Image evidence for a
workload built by a consuming language agent belongs to that agent, which binds
it to the digest and platform it actually built; the generic toolbox never
reports image coverage on another agent's behalf.
